Well, as I indicated, I was pretty upset as I wrote that; I should know
better, I guess.  Anyway, the point was not that a different form of
posting would be better (I doubt it), but that the addition of a brik-
style Checksum: line to a text posting can let us know immediately if
the posting is okay or not.  Most of the trouble I have had with the
Nethack distribution was caused by some system inserting apparently
random newlines here and there.  These sometimes become obvious right
away when they cause illegal syntax.  Sometimes they just create
oddness in the application of subsequent patches.  They leave me
uncertain that I have what I think I have.  A portable checksum would
help me with this, and let me request reposts or whatever in a timely
fashion.

As it is, I have been trying to reconstruct the original postings by
a process of deduction.

The stuff after the #!/bin/sh line was not meant to be intelligible
until unpacked.  The stuff after #!/bin/sh in the Nethack distribution
is apparently never meant to be intelligible to people at all :-).
The fact that some folks continue to gain enlightenment, or at least
spoilers, from perusing it is a continuing testimonial to the
dedication with which some folks pursue the difficult.


